
# MicML #####################################################################

This is an example of sound processing with the ESP32. It is a bit
**out-of-date**, so best check the course notes [section on
Marvin](https://iot.unphone.net/#sec:marvin) or [my fork of Chris G's
code](https://github.com/hamishcunningham/diy-alexa) instead.


## Note on builds ###########################################################

At this version it compiles with pio, magic.sh (IDF 4.3) and ArdIDE:

> commit 5e14af20f5056c85b180f7816bfdfa024a546505 (HEAD -> master, origin/master, origin/HEAD)
> Date:   Fri Feb 12 14:45:25 2021 +0000

Beyond this is likely won't run properly with IDF 4.3 (triggers server comms bug).


## New version: Chris Greening's ICS-43434 mic board ########################

Code from [his github
here](https://github.com/atomic14/ICS-43434-breakout-board).

Attempts to communicate with [a node server here](server/).

To (re-)create [the lib/tfmicro
tree](https://gitlab.com/hamishcunningham/the-internet-of-things/-/tree/master/exercises/MicML)
in MicML [follow his instructions
here](https://github.com/atomic14/platformio-tensorflow-lite).
